// pfodWeb NOTE (button/LED/NeoPixel tagging + dedicated-hardware pin
// exclusion audit, 2026-07-13):
//
// Board: DatanoiseTV PicoADK (RP2040) - a real audio-synthesis/effects
// development board built around an onboard PCM5102/PCM5100A-family
// 32-bit I2S DAC/audio codec (the vendor's own README uses both chip
// names for the same codec), plus 4 debug LEDs near the USB connector,
// a separate "Big Debug LED", a VBUS-detect pin, and an onboard 8-channel
// SPI ADC (ADC128) whose bus is also shared out to the pin headers. This
// arduino-pico "datanoisetv_picoadk" board id (build.board=
// DATANOISETV_PICOADK) is the original RP2040 PicoADK - distinct from
// the separate RP2350-based "datanoisetv_picoadk_v2" board id, which is
// out of scope for this audit (its own variants/rp2040/rp2350/
// datanoisetv_picoadk_v2/ tree is a different chip bucket entirely).
//
// Sources consulted (WebSearch/WebFetch, 2026-07-13):
//  1. https://github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Hardware (main repo; the
//     pins_arduino.h header comment's cited source,
//     github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoDSP-Hardware, now redirects/renamed to
//     this repo).
//  2. https://github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Hardware/blob/main/README.md
//     - the authoritative "Internal Signals" GPIO table. Quoted directly:
//     "GPIO2".."GPIO5" = "Debug LED 1".."Debug LED 4" ("shared w/
//     Header"); "GPIO10".."GPIO13" = SPI1/ADC128 SCK/MOSI/MISO/CSn
//     ("shared w/ Header"); "GPIO15" = "Big Debug LED (WS2812 on v1.1a)"
//     (NOT shared w/ header); "GPIO16","GPIO17","GPIO18" = PCM5100A I2S
//     DAT/BCLK/LRCLK; "GPIO23" = "PCM5100A DEMP"; "GPIO24" = "VBUS Detect
//     Pin"; "GPIO25" = "PCM5102 XSMT". Also: "The analog lineout pins...
//     I2S pins are exposed on the headers, to allow for connecting an
//     ADC" and "Make sure your software controls the XSMT and DEMP pins.
//     The XSMT needs to be controlled by the software to mute/unmute the
//     audio output."
//  3. https://github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Hardware/blob/main/GettingStarted_Arduino.md
//     - Arduino code samples. Confirms active-high polarity for the
//     debug LED bank: `pinMode(PIN_LED0, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(PIN_LED0,
//     1);` turns PIN_LED0 on. Also shows `pinMode(pDemp, OUTPUT);
//     digitalWrite(pDemp, LOW);` (GPIO23/DEMP) and
//     `pinMode(pMute, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(pMute, HIGH);` (GPIO25/XSMT)
//     as plain software-driven control outputs, not general I/O.
//  4. This board's own variants/rp2040/rp2040/datanoisetv_picoadk/pins_arduino.h
//     (bespoke/flattened, no ../generic/common.h include - the raw
//     upstream copy at rp2040_board_variants/variants/datanoisetv_picoadk/
//     pins_arduino.h does include it, confirming this variant's own
//     comment on GPIO16-19 - "SPI0, which this ... board reuses as the
//     I2S bus" - was deliberately authored for this repo, not
//     auto-generated).
//  5. variants/rp2040/rp2040/board.json (chip-level defaults,
//     chipGpios: {}), variants/rp2040/rp2040/rpipico/board.json and
//     variants/rp2040/rp2040/adafruit_macropad2040/board.json
//     (sparse-override structural precedent; macropad also established
//     the "add capabilities:[] purely for documentation even when a pin
//     is already excluded by having no D-alias" convention followed
//     here for GPIO16-19/23-25).
//     variants/esp32/esp32c6/makergo_c6_supermini/board.json (established
//     "leave untagged / NO CHANGE rather than guess" convention for a
//     confirmed-onboard-LED whose exact drive characteristics could not
//     be confirmed from available sources - followed here for GPIO15).
//  6. pfodWeb_src/build_boards.js (buildEsp32Board()/parseEsp32Consts()) -
//     confirmed the i2c_sda/i2c_scl/spi_ss/spi_mosi/spi_miso/spi_sck
//     auto-append only fires off the UNQUALIFIED `consts.SDA`/`SCL`/
//     `SS`/`MOSI`/`MISO`/`SCK` static-const aliases. This board's header
//     declares only `SDA`/`SCL` (via PIN_WIRE0_SDA/SCL, GPIO8/9) as
//     unqualified aliases - no SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK unqualified alias exists
//     anywhere in this header (only the PIN_SPI0_*/PIN_SPI1_* qualified
//     #defines), so the "confirmed button/LED pin also aliased as
//     SDA/SCL/SS/MOSI/MISO/SCK" bug class flagged in this audit's task
//     brief was checked and does NOT fire on this board - GPIO8/GPIO9
//     (the only pins carrying the SDA/SCL auto-tag) are ordinary
//     general-purpose/header pins, not tagged button/LED, so there is no
//     collision to fix.
//
// GPIO2/3/4/5 (PIN_LED0-PIN_LED3, "Debug LED 1"-"Debug LED 4" per source
// #2, "shared w/ Header"): CHANGED - each tagged
// ["digital_output","pwm_output","led_high"]. Active-high polarity
// directly confirmed for PIN_LED0 via source #3's
// `digitalWrite(PIN_LED0, 1)` turning it on; PIN_LED1-3 inferred to
// share the same polarity as PIN_LED0 (identical debug-LED bank, same
// schematic pattern), not independently confirmed per-pin - flagged
// here rather than treated as a separate independent source. digital_input
// dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent (rpipico,
// adafruit_macropad2040, akana_r1). These remain also usable as ordinary
// header-exposed GPIO per source #2's "shared w/ Header" note, matching
// how LED_BUILTIN pins elsewhere in this repo keep pwm_output despite
// also being a dedicated onboard LED.
//
// GPIO15 (PIN_LED, "Big Debug LED (WS2812 on v1.1a)" per source #2, NOT
// shared w/ header): NO CHANGE - left at chip-level default capability
// (no chipGpios entry added). Confirmed dedicated (not header-exposed),
// but source #2's own parenthetical flags this as a WS2812 addressable
// RGB LED specifically "on v1.1a" hardware, while the arduino-pico core
// exposes only a single unversioned "datanoisetv_picoadk" board id
// (this board's own boards.txt entry lists 8 different USB VID/PID
// pairs across multiple upload_port entries, consistent with one
// Arduino board id spanning several hardware sub-revisions). No source
// found confirms whether every hardware revision reachable via this
// single board id uses the WS2812 (vs. a plain single-colour LED on
// earlier v1.0/v1.1 boards, implied by the "(WS2812 on v1.1a)"
// qualifier existing at all). Tagging led_neopixel would be wrong for a
// plain-LED revision (WS2812's PIO-driven one-wire protocol won't just
// light up under a bare digitalWrite); tagging led_high would be wrong
// for a WS2812 revision (a sustained digitalWrite(HIGH) does not
// register as a valid WS2812 data frame - the LED will not reliably
// light). Per this repo's established
// leave-untagged-rather-than-guess convention (esp32c6/
// makergo_c6_supermini's GPIO15, ambiguous LED drive polarity), this
// pin is flagged here for a future dedicated hardware-revision-specific
// pass rather than guessed. D15 alias already exists in pins_arduino.h,
// so it continues to appear as a normal digital_input/digital_output/
// pwm_output pin, same as before this audit.
//
// GPIO16 (PIN_SPI0_MISO / PIN_I2S_DOUT), GPIO17 (PIN_SPI0_SS /
// PIN_I2S_BCLK), GPIO18 (PIN_SPI0_SCK / PIN_I2S_LRCLK): CHANGED
// (excluded). capabilities: [] each. Dedicated I2S data/bit-clock/
// word-select lines to the onboard PCM5102/PCM5100A audio codec,
// confirmed via source #2's table (GPIO16/17/18 = I2S DAT/BCLK/LRCLK).
// None has a static-const D-alias in this board's pins_arduino.h (its
// own inline comment: "D16-D19 deliberately NOT declared... GPIO16-19
// are SPI0, which this ... board reuses as the I2S bus... not
// general-purpose") - already invisible/excluded by default; explicit
// chipGpios entries added purely for documentation, matching the
// adafruit_macropad2040 OLED-bus/piezo-speaker documentation pattern.
//
// GPIO19 (PIN_SPI0_MOSI): CHANGED (excluded). capabilities: []. The 4th
// wire of the same SPI0 peripheral block reused for I2S above. Source
// #2's own Internal Signals table does not separately name GPIO19 (only
// DAT/BCLK/LRCLK on GPIO16/17/18 are listed as I2S signals) - this
// board's playback-only I2S DAC has no DIN/data-in need for a 4th wire,
// so GPIO19 is plausibly an unused/spare pin of the SPI0 block rather
// than an independently-confirmed dedicated line. It is excluded here
// anyway, matching this board's own pins_arduino.h comment which already
// groups all of GPIO16-19 together as "SPI0" reused for I2S (no D19
// alias declared either) - not re-opening a wire the header's own author
// already treated as part of the reused peripheral block, consistent
// with this repo's established whole-bus-exclusion precedent for
// dedicated internal SPI buses (wiznet_*_evb_pico* Ethernet SPI, GPIO26-28
// on adafruit_macropad2040's OLED SPI1).
//
// GPIO23 (PCM5100A DEMP - deemphasis control): CHANGED (excluded).
// capabilities: []. Dedicated software-driven control output to the
// onboard codec (per source #2's table entry and source #3's
// `pinMode(pDemp, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(pDemp, LOW);` example). No
// static-const alias exists anywhere in this board's pins_arduino.h -
// was already invisible/excluded by default; entry added purely for
// documentation.
//
// GPIO24 (VBUS Detect Pin): CHANGED (excluded). capabilities: [].
// Dedicated hardware-sense line reading USB VBUS presence, per source
// #2's table. No static-const alias in pins_arduino.h - same
// already-excluded/documentation-only treatment as GPIO23/25.
//
// GPIO25 (PCM5102 XSMT - mute/unmute control): CHANGED (excluded).
// capabilities: []. Dedicated software-driven mute-control output to
// the onboard codec (per source #2's table entry and source #3's
// `pinMode(pMute, OUTPUT); digitalWrite(pMute, HIGH);` example, and
// source #2's explicit "The XSMT needs to be controlled by the software
// to mute/unmute the audio output"). No static-const alias in
// pins_arduino.h - same treatment as GPIO23/24.
//
// GPIO0/1 (Serial1 TX/RX), GPIO6/7 (Wire1 SDA/SCL), GPIO8/9 (Serial2
// TX/RX, doubling as Wire0 SDA/SCL), GPIO10-13 (SPI1, doubling as the
// onboard ADC128's SPI bus - source #2: "The SPI ADC shares the GPIO10
// to GPIO13, which are also present on the pin headers"), GPIO14,
// GPIO20-22, GPIO26-28 (A0-A2): NO CHANGE. All ordinary
// general-purpose/header-exposed pins per source #2's own "shared w/
// Header" language (for GPIO10-13) or simply absent from every internal-
// signal source consulted (GPIO0/1, 6/7, 8/9, 14, 20-22, 26-28). Left at
// full chip-default capability. GPIO8/GPIO9 do carry the unqualified
// SDA/SCL static-const aliases (auto-tagged i2c_sda/i2c_scl by
// build_boards.js), which is expected/correct behaviour for a
// general-purpose I2C pin, not a collision (see source #6 above).
//
// Full findings/sources trail:
// boardsDetails/rp2040/rp2040/datanoisetv_picoadk/notes.txt
{
  // Output filename and BoardLoader data-variable name:
  //   boardName "RP2040" -> designer/boards/RP2040/RP2040.json -> const RP2040Data = {...}
  "boardName": "RP2040",

  // Fallback human-readable name shown in the designer UI.  Overridden
  // by the matching `<id>.name=` entry in a sibling-or-ancestor
  // boards.txt when one is present (matched via `<id>.build.variant=`
  // against this variant's directory name).
  "displayName": "Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040)",

  // Same parser dialect as every other RP2040 board - see
  // ../board.json for the full rationale.
  "family": "rp2040",

  // This board's debug LEDs and codec-control lines are ordinary
  // software-driven GPIO outputs (per the vendor's own Arduino code
  // samples), not capacitive/input-only pins - handled entirely via the
  // chipGpios entries below, so no inputOnlyGpios entry is needed.
  "inputOnlyGpios": [],

  // Default transports - Serial only (plain RP2040 chip bucket, no
  // onboard WiFi chip).
  "connections": ["serial"],

  "pinNotes": {},

  "chipGpios": {
    "2":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED0 - \"Debug LED 1\" near the USB connector, shared w/ header. Confirmed active-high via github.com/DatanoiseTV/PicoADK-Hardware GettingStarted_Arduino.md: digitalWrite(PIN_LED0, 1) turns it on." },
    "3":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED1 - \"Debug LED 2\" near the USB connector, shared w/ header. Polarity inferred to match PIN_LED0 (GPIO2), same debug-LED bank - not independently confirmed per-pin." },
    "4":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED2 - \"Debug LED 3\" near the USB connector, shared w/ header. Polarity inferred to match PIN_LED0 (GPIO2), same debug-LED bank - not independently confirmed per-pin." },
    "5":  { "capabilities": ["digital_output", "pwm_output", "led_high"], "note": "PIN_LED3 - \"Debug LED 4\" near the USB connector, shared w/ header. Polarity inferred to match PIN_LED0 (GPIO2), same debug-LED bank - not independently confirmed per-pin." },
    "16": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SPI0_MISO / PIN_I2S_DOUT - dedicated I2S data line to the onboard PCM5102/PCM5100A audio codec. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "17": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SPI0_SS / PIN_I2S_BCLK - dedicated I2S bit-clock line to the onboard audio codec. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "18": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SPI0_SCK / PIN_I2S_LRCLK - dedicated I2S word-select (LR clock) line to the onboard audio codec. No static-const alias in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "19": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PIN_SPI0_MOSI - 4th wire of the SPI0 peripheral block reused for I2S above (GPIO16-18). Not separately named in the vendor's own I2S signal list (playback-only DAC has no DIN need), but grouped here with the rest of the reused SPI0 block per this board's own pins_arduino.h comment, which already excludes it (no D19 alias declared)." },
    "23": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PCM5100A DEMP - deemphasis control output to the onboard audio codec, software-driven (pinMode(OUTPUT); digitalWrite(...)) per vendor's GettingStarted_Arduino.md example. No static-const alias anywhere in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "24": { "capabilities": [], "note": "VBUS Detect Pin - dedicated hardware-sense line reading USB VBUS presence, per vendor's PicoADK-Hardware README Internal Signals table. No static-const alias anywhere in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." },
    "25": { "capabilities": [], "note": "PCM5102 XSMT - mute/unmute control output to the onboard audio codec, software-driven per vendor's GettingStarted_Arduino.md example and README (\"The XSMT needs to be controlled by the software to mute/unmute the audio output\"). No static-const alias anywhere in this board's pins_arduino.h; entry added for documentation." }
  },

  // Same 8-bit analogWrite() default as every other RP2040/RP2350 board.
  "pwm": { "min": 0, "max": 255, "method": "analogWrite" },

  // No hardware DAC on RP2040/RP2350 (this board's 32-bit audio output
  // comes from the onboard I2S PCM5102/PCM5100A codec chip, not the
  // RP2040's own silicon, so the chip-level "no DAC" fact still holds).
  "dac": {},

  // 3 analog channels (A0-A2 = GPIO26-28), 12-bit ADC - matches the
  // chip-level default and this board's own pins_arduino.h
  // (NUM_ANALOG_INPUTS=3, ADC_RESOLUTION=12).
  "adc": { "bits": 12, "max": 4095, "defaultRefVolts": "3.3" }
}
